{
  "$comment": [
    "The names each package is imported by (docs/boundary.md, \"Entries\"). Each entry is the name an importer writes: its layer, the module it starts at (`source`) and the file its types are read from (`types`).",
    "`packages` are the workspaces under packages/, each owning its sources: a module's layer is the package it sits in. Each entry is in its package's `exports`, pointed at its source; `node scripts/check-boundary.mjs --entries` holds the manifests and each entry's import closure to it. The database browser (`tablewalk`) publishes none of the App framework's names: an App imports `mistri/*`, and the browser installs and runs without mistri.",
    "The JSON schemas under `./schema/*.json` are files, not modules: mistri owns and publishes them."
  ],
  "packages": {
    "@mistriwork/engine": { "dir": "packages/engine", "layer": "engine" },
    "@mistriwork/ui": { "dir": "packages/ui", "layer": "ui" },
    "@mistriwork/kit": { "dir": "packages/kit", "layer": "kit" },
    "@mistriwork/mistri": { "dir": "packages/mistri", "layer": "mistri" },
    "create-mistri": { "dir": "packages/create-mistri", "layer": "mistri" },
    "@mistriwork/cloudflare": { "dir": "packages/cloudflare", "layer": "cloudflare" },
    "tablewalk": { "dir": "packages/tablewalk", "layer": "browser" }
  },
  "entries": {
